From f054760c86f47f6394dd896a816a8ffcdb24a70e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:34:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(worker): back the KV cache with the GB10 display
 carve-out

DGX Spark firmware reserves about 2 GiB at the top of physical memory for
display scanout. Ordinary allocations never use it, and a text console takes
only its framebuffer (8 MiB at 1920x1080). With SPARK3_KV_DISPLAY_CARVEOUT=1
the worker takes the whole KV cache backing from a DRM dumb buffer in that
carve-out, exported as a dma-buf and imported with cuImportExternalMemory.

Measured on GB10: the imported mapping reads at 235 GB/s against 252 GB/s for
cudaMalloc (a torch copy runs at the same rate as ordinary memory), while
registering the CPU mapping as I/O memory reads at 164 GB/s. Data written by
the GPU and CPU round-trips without mismatches. The worker refuses to start
if the carve-out cannot hold the backing, so the cache never falls back into
ordinary memory.
